		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=17243&amp;sid=4304614022e574f73f9afd830d3dbc09#17243"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Tue Apr 27, 2004 10:32 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=17243&amp;sid=4304614022e574f73f9afd830d3dbc09"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Schmanks.. they've been a handful so far. Fun, but a handful... 
<br />

<br />
And I hear ya about only being able to pay for one online addiction. <img src="images/smiles/icon_smile.gif" alt="icon_smile.gif" border="0" /> It's one reason why my husband and I decided to drop EQ, well, that and he hadn't played for months and we started playing EQ for something to do together. I do miss the people I knew on D-ro, and I'll be honest I even sometimes miss the timesink that EQ becomes. However, I don't ever want to say in my life that I miss the time I could have spent with my family and right now my girls really need me, EQ or WoW or whatever next great thing comes along. 
<br />

<br />
I do plan on checking WoW out, as I've heard excellent things about it (a friend of mine has a beta account) but I honestly think that my time with major involvement in MMORPG's is over. One nice thing that I hope survives beta tho is the idea of a sliding scale of xp. Once you're on for a certain number of hours, wham! any bonuses you had to xp are gone.. for example, you start off with say a 200% bonus to your xp. After 8 hours, that bonus drops.. drastically, until you log off for at least 8 hours. Personally, I think it's a pretty slick way to help the casual gamer keep up with the power gamer, and it might mean that the power gamer has more characters at a higher level, but it means that I can keep up with my one or two characters. That and I really like the idea of being there at the beginning of the game instead of having to play catch up... 
<br />

<br />
Hope everything's going well on your end, and I'll see what I can do about popping in to help stir up some trouble. <img src="images/smiles/icon_smile.gif" alt="icon_smile.gif" border="0" /></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
